# rmb-desktop releases

When the user asks to cut, ship, publish, or deploy a release — or when a fix is ready for the remote instance — **run the release pipeline yourself**. Do not ask permission to upload to GitHub.

## One command

```bash
cd /Users/liguanghui/Virginia/colinleefish/rmb-desktop
SIGN_KEYCHAIN_PASS='rmb-sign' make release VERSION=0.1.x
```

Or upload an already-built DMG:

```bash
UPLOAD_ONLY=1 make release VERSION=0.1.x
```

Credentials live in `~/.rmb/release.env` (see `scripts/release.env.example`). Prefer sourcing that file over prompting.

## Pipeline (automatic)

1. `make app-build` — signed Tauri build
2. `make notarize` — Apple notarization + staple
3. `scripts/release.sh` — verify staple, upload DMG to GitHub (create or clobber)

Optional: `PUBLISH_R2=1` pushes to `releases.re-mem-ber.me` via sibling `rmb-website` repo.

## Version bumps

Before releasing, update `VERSION` in:
- `Makefile` (default `VERSION ?=`)
- `app/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` (`package.version`)

Commit the version bump only when the user asks.

## After upload

- Confirm release URL: `https://github.com/colinleefish/rmb-desktop/releases/tag/vX.Y.Z`
- Remote test host (`10.254.24.7:19019`): user installs DMG manually unless they ask you to deploy via SSH
